<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the signed desktop app (#2761, ADR-0122 D-H3).
  The bundler passes this file to codesign through
  `tauri.conf.json > bundle > macOS > entitlements`.

  Keep it to what the app actually needs. WKWebView's JIT runs in WebKit's own
  WebContent process, so it does not belong here.

  The bundler signs the momo-workd sidecar with this same file. So it holds no
  restricted entitlement (application-identifier, keychain-access-groups):
  those need a provisioning profile, which a bare sidecar binary cannot carry,
  and the device-key group is the app's alone (ADR-0146 D-3). The signed app
  gets them from Entitlements.app.plist, which scripts/publish_next_build.sh
  applies to the outer .app after embedding the profile. The legacy login
  keychain the sign-in token uses needs no entitlement.

  com.apple.security.device.audio-input: huddle microphone. Under the hardened
  runtime, TCC denies the microphone without showing a prompt when this is
  missing. The prompt text is NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
